and drove the real attempt-3 snapshot end-to-end rather than trusting the
diff claim alone.

## Method

Built `go build ./cmd/server` from the WS4.3 snapshot (no `.git`), ran it
on 127.0.0.1:55895 against a `cp -rL` copy of `/home/darrell/bin/ai/
budget2/data` (BUDGET2_BACKUP_DIR/IMPORT_DIR under scratch, BUDGET_DEBUG=
false) — never :8080, never a repo-root binary. Drove it with real
Playwright (Chromium, NODE_PATH=.../e41f203b7505f1fb/node_modules)
against the live templates/JS/handlers, corroborated with `axe` (@axe-
core/cli 4.13.0, `--chrome-options=blink-settings=preferredColorScheme=
1|2`) and `go test`/`node --test`. Server killed after (confirmed down:
curl → connection refused).

## 1. Retargeted Add-form rejections, both themes — PASS (ACCESSIBILITY.md
   point 5 / WCAG 4.1.3)

Income (live, real server, inverted date range via a later start_month,
avoiding native `min`-attribute blocking): FIRST rejection, SECOND
identical rejection, and a THIRD *different-message* rejection, light +
dark — alert-count stayed exactly 1 throughout (no nesting, no
re-duplication):
```
PASS A1 income FIRST (light/dark)   before=0 after=1
PASS A2 income SECOND identical     count=1 (no re-announce)
PASS A4 income DIFFERENT message    count=1 (re-announced, not duplicated)
```
`ariaSnapshot()` of `#whatif-add-income-error` confirms structure and
non-nesting directly:
```
- alert:
  - img
  - text: Error
  - paragraph: Through month cannot be before the start month
```
Expense (live, real server, same inverted-range technique): FIRST
rejection alert-count=1, both themes.

Bigticket/onetime/healthcare (route-intercepted 400 carrying the real
`renderError` fragment shape and `HX-Retarget` header, all required
fields filled first so the client doesn't block submission itself): all
three, both themes, alert-count=1. This is the same technique the
attempt-2 verdict used for its synthetic-5xx case, applied here because
their business-rule rejection triggers are less direct to reach from the
DOM than a date-range check — it exercises the identical client
announcement/dedupe logic (`errorHost`/`buildErrorNode`/`findMarked`) as
a real server 400 would.

## 2. Non-retargeted edit-row rejection (income, Through before Starts) —
   LIVE, PASS

First attempt at this hit htmx's *native* HTML5 constraint validation
(`htmx:validation:halted`) because both `start_month`/`end_month` share
one `min` attribute — pushing `end_month` below it blocks the request
client-side before it ever reaches the server. Retried with the same
later-start technique as the Add forms (both fields stay ≥ `min`, only
start > end triggers the server's 400): real PUT fired, 400 returned,
single `[data-wf-inline-error]`/`role="alert"` node, both themes:
```
PASS D1 edit-row rejection (light/dark)   marked=1 alerts=1
PASS D2 focus stayed on the edited end_month input (light/dark)
```

## 3. Synthetic 5xx and text/plain error body — PASS

Route-intercepted `POST /whatif/onetime`: a 500 with a renderError-shaped
HTML body → single alert (count=1). A second run returning a bare
`text/plain` panic body → still single alert via the JS's textContent
fallback path (`buildErrorNode`), no throw, no duplicate.

## 4. Poll sentinel — PASS

Route-intercepted `GET /whatif/poll**` → 500 continuously across two real
2s poll cycles (4.5s wait): grid child count unchanged (3→3), zero
`[data-wf-inline-error]` nodes anywhere — the poll never re-announces.

## 5. Page-load silence — PASS

Fresh `/whatif` load: 0 `[role="alert"]` nodes.

